# Environment setup.
#
# The app reads VITE_SUPABASE_URL / VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY. To keep local
# development off the production database, use Vite's mode-specific env files:
#
#   .env.development  → STAGING project   (used by `npm run dev`)
#   .env.production   → PRODUCTION project (used by `npm run build`)
#   .env              → shared, non-secret defaults (the login gate)
#
# On Vercel, set the production Supabase vars in the dashboard — those drive the
# deployed app. All of these .env files are gitignored (except this example).
#
# Copy this file to each of the above and fill in the matching project values.

# Supabase — Project Settings → API (use the STAGING project in .env.development,
# the PRODUCTION project in .env.production)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# Predefined login for the app (single-user gate) — can be shared across envs
VITE_APP_USERNAME=admin
VITE_APP_PASSWORD=lernen
